<title>CANADA: Canadian dollar ends firmer ahead of budget.</title>
<headline>Canadian dollar ends firmer ahead of budget.</headline>
<text>
<p>FORECAST RANGE   1.3540/1.3580	    ASIAN CLOSE     1.3533</p>
<p>RESISTANCE 1.3470   SUPPORT 1.3580	HI 1.3575   LO  1.3420</p>
<p>CANADA OPEN  1.3565/70    HI 1.3590     EUROPE OPEN     1.3554</p>
<p>PREV CLOSE   1.3514/19    LO 1.3520     HI 1.3565   LO  1.3525</p>
<p>----------------------MARKET COMMENT--------------------------</p>
<p>* The Canadian dollar closed out the regular trading day firmer at C$1.3548 from this morning's open of around C$1.3563 (US$0.7372) and much stronger than midday lows around C$1.3572 (US$0.7368) ahead of the Canadian government's budget for the the fiscal year 1997/98 at 1630 EST (2130 GMT).</p>
<p>((Paul Casciato, Reuters Toronto Bureau 416 941-8100 or email: paul.casciato@reuters.com))</p>
